{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned","id":1164313,"title":"Let's Read Half Damned","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-01T10:02:53-08:00","id":1164313,"title":"Let's Read Half Damned","content":"Because that book looks cool enough, and I waited for it long enough, and I always wanted to make such a thread :P<br /> <br /> <b><u>Table of Content</u></b><br /> <br /> Dhampirs, Revenants and Ghouls. No surprises in here. Seems to be much more in depth than what I expected- which is always a good thing.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Introduction</u></b><br /> <br /> Good opening. Making a quick yet strong impression of who the &quot;half damned&quot; are and their place in the setting. Nice.<br /> <br /> Strange that they start with dhampirs as the first chapter and ghouls as the last. I assume they wanted to put the &quot;cool and new&quot; at the front. Still, strange.<br /> <br /> Ohh I do like the all &quot;children who were never meant to be born, and as such become tuned to fate&quot; thing which goes for dhampirs. Cool. Really cool.<br /> <br /> Themes of family and rebellion.. so being a dhampir is being an eternal teenager? :P<br /> <br /> Again the Omen thing. Really gives a &quot;Child of Misfortune&quot; feeling. I like it.<br /> <br /> Revenants- again, an whole isolation and outcast themes. I must say, the Revenant really do feel like a &quot;Wicked Dead&quot;, even though they didn't showed up in that book. Good thing they were added in 2e.<br /> <br /> Being a revenant seems to be a sad, sad existence, even more than I imagined. It feels like the book did really managed to give a solid reason for why revenants <i>need</i> a supplement instead of being &quot;just&quot; a sidebar about a weird phenomena/antagonist.<br /> <br /> Finally- ghouls. I wonder if the phanariots would get an honorary mention in here (not likely, but one can hope!).<br /> <br /> Selfish servants who are bound to their regnant? Sounds like a good description of what a &quot;ghoul&quot; is.<br /> <br /> And for a word from our sponsors (inspirational media!)-<br /> <br /> So each lesser template gets its own media? Makes sense.<br /> <br /> For Dhampirs:<br /> <br /> Vampire Hunter D- always saw the AMV, never saw the anime. Maybe I should.<br /> <br /> Blade, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Angel? cool.<br /> <br /> For Revenants:<br /> <br /> never heard of any of those. Oh well.<br /> <br /> For Ghouls:<br /> <br /> Dracula. Colour me surprise *sarcasm*<br /> <br /> Other CofD:<br /> <br /> Ghouls- like, duh?<br /> <br /> Wicked Dead- one of my favorites.<br /> <br /> <b><u>We are going for commercials- Fiction</u></b><br /> <br /> A strong, black woman fucks with a two dimensional villain. Its kinda cool and easy to read, and kinda cement the dhampir condition- but it is kinda too on the nose. Still, there is only so much you can do in an opening fiction, right?<br /> <br /> Well, I need to go to eat. Chapter 1 would, obviously, come next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T02:24:13-08:00","id":1164488,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Chapter I- Dhampirs</u></b><br /> <br /> Now the <i>real</i> fun can begin.<br /> <br /> A GoT quote. Cool.<br /> <br /> A passage for justifying the dhampir's place in the setting.<br /> <br /> I must say I'm not sure about all of this &quot;vampire demonization&quot;, but as this is all presented from the dhampiric PoV I can accept it.<br /> <br /> So the act of making a dhampir is a selfish one. Well, its not like it is the natural mean of reproduction for the undead :P<br /> <br /> &quot;where the Embrace is sometimes forbidden, making a dhampir rarely is&quot;- of course, because who would have thought you would be stupid enough for that?<br /> <br /> wait.. so <i>Success </i>on the Attachment role means you can say &quot;fuck the child, throw it to the genesis lab&quot;? Yikes.<br /> <br /> I wonder if a &quot;mortal and a vampire&quot; still means what it meant in Wicked Dead. You know, the poor mortal guy who got a dhampir in his belly.<br /> <br /> I can accept that Embraced pregnant women have a chance to birth a vampire- but how exactly the curse vector move from a father to the womb of a future mother? I assume it works more or less through the other ways the Beast &quot;embody&quot; itself in others, but still, a bit complicated process.<br /> <br /> <b>Random thought</b>- what would happen if a strix ridden vampire would try to make a dhampir? The strix do have Curac, after all.<br /> <br /> So the presented rituals work only when biology agrees with sorcery. Ha. In my table, those rituals would be the &quot;safe&quot; options, which the ones from Wicked Dead as the more.. drastic ones.<br /> <br /> So the Covenants generally accept the existence of dhampirs? They have their reasons, I assume. Oh, here are their reasons-<br /> <br /> Carthians- there is a strength in numbers. You are a number.<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone- Behold the miracle of unholy birth!<br /> <br /> (be careful of the scary midwives)<br /> <br /> Invictus- You are not a part of the All Night Society. You are its property.<br /> <br /> Half Blood Director- because &quot;Prince&quot; was taken (still, cool plot hook).<br /> <br /> Lancea et Sanctum- Dark Jesus Reborn, the holy scourge of God!<br /> <br /> (I must say it is like 180 degrees away from their view in Wicked Dead- and from what it is said in the Testament of Longinus. I assume that the Church of the Damned would have its own reasoning for why they do not butcher dhampirs as they were commanded).<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul- what a beautiful subject of research...<br /> <br /> Well, the Covenants seems to mostly embrace the concept of half breed children- but society is one thing. What about their own family? Let's check!<br /> <br /> So occult genesis is still genesis?<br /> <br /> Daeva- sit there and be beautiful, my little puppet.<br /> <br /> Gangrel- Survive or die is the all law.<br /> <br /> Mekhet- Let's play a game..<br /> <br /> Nosferatu- Give mommy a kiss, she loves you<br /> <br /> Ventrue- I told you 100 times- Dinner comes <i>after</i> you finish playing Mozart's Violin Concerto. You always miss the last note. I don't care that your fingers are bleeding! Now, hurry up. The food is getting cold.<br /> <br /> Oooooh, a Crossover section. I like that.<br /> <br /> Werewolves- That which was never meant to be has to be culled- unless they proof they are meant to be.<br /> <br /> Mages- What a nice Mystery to solve!<br /> <br /> Changeling- You need a place to hide. I know where.<br /> <br /> Demons- You are <i>wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> What? No Beasts? In a Crossover section made for a splat which has the theme of <i>Family</i>? What a missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, that's a time to take a break. I'll continue from here next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-02-2017, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T07:34:30-08:00","id":1165042,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Dhampir- Part 2!</u></b><br /> <br /> So the childhood of a dhampir is messed up. Who would have thought?<br /> <br /> I must say that there seems to be a lot in common between the Lucifuge and dhampirs. I wonder if Hunter 2e would refer to it.<br /> <br /> Seriously- couldn't they just say whether dhampirs can or can not make more of their kind through regular breeding? I would say no, and that they &quot;simply&quot; gain certain supernatural merits instead of a dhampir template, but still it is not something that sounds like it would be a mystery in setting. I'm sure at least one Dragon has done such an experiment.<br /> <br /> I assume Masquerade doesn't have a monopoly over the Chess metaphor, but it still kinda made me feel more M than R.<br /> <br /> I don't know, up until now it feels like the way vampires have been portrayed in this book is really different from how they were seen in 2e- a lot more dead and monstrous, that is. Again, I assume that it is because dhampirs experience things different from the Kindred, but in 2e they felt so much more.. alive, and I kinda miss that in that section.<br /> <br /> &quot;does he think he loves it&quot;- yet another example of the lack of passion I miss so much.<br /> <br /> Yeah, yeah, having a dhampir is a bad idea... too much word count about why a vampire who makes dhampirs is an idiot, I think.<br /> <br /> general feeling until now is that the text has spend too much about saying why being a dhampir sucks. I want it to focus more about why being dhampir is awesome instead.<br /> <br /> &quot;guardian devil&quot;. That's cool.<br /> <br /> Will we get something more substantial about all the &quot;purpose&quot; thingy, or is it just a RP thing?<br /> <br /> Haven't we already covered how vampires feels toward their children?<br /> <br /> Haven't we already covered how dhampirs act in the All Night Society in the same section?<br /> <br /> Really, up until now I personally don't really enjoy that section. I hope the next would be better.<br /> <br /> wait- so are there many dhampirs who work as hunters or aren't? It looks like each passage claims it to be otherwise...<br /> <br /> So dhampirs are the horror stories vampires tell each other when they go for camping in the mountains? Now, that's cool!<br /> <br /> I must say that considering the many hunter references, I'm surprised that Hunter didn't showed up in the Crossover section.<br /> <br /> The Boogeymen sound really cool. Now we are back on the track. I wonder if they could be styled as a compact/conspiracy<br /> <br /> So dhampirs can't make of their own kind. Then why did they kept it a mystery earlier? Anyway, the last section was much better written than the previous one, IMO.<br /> <br /> Well, that's not much, but I have homework in Quantum Mechanics to do, so I'll stop here before I'll start reviewing the Character Creation part. As this post was kinda more harsh than I usually make, feel free to disagree with everything I said :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T08:45:39-08:00","id":1165061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1164488#post1164488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;where the Embrace is sometimes forbidden, making a dhampir rarely is&quot;- of course, because who would have thought you would be stupid enough for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also suspect most vampires don't even think having children is possible. You don't generally need a law against the impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> wait.. so <i>Success </i>on the Attachment role means you can say &quot;fuck the child, throw it to the genesis lab&quot;? Yikes. </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. The roll is about whether an unwanted attachement forms despite the dhampir being made for some other purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T08:58:20-08:00","id":1165063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165042#post1165042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Dhampir- Part 2!</u></b><br /> <br /> So the childhood of a dhampir is messed up. Who would have thought?<br /> <br /> I must say that there seems to be a lot in common between the Lucifuge and dhampirs. I wonder if Hunter 2e would refer to it.<br /> <br /> Seriously- couldn't they just say whether dhampirs can or can not make more of their kind through regular breeding? I would say no, and that they &amp;quot;simply&amp;quot; gain certain supernatural merits instead of a dhampir template, but still it is not something that sounds like it would be a mystery in setting. I'm sure at least one Dragon has done such an experiment.<br /> <br /> I assume Masquerade doesn't have a monopoly over the Chess metaphor, but it still kinda made me feel more M than R.<br /> <br /> I don't know, up until now it feels like the way vampires have been portrayed in this book is really different from how they were seen in 2e- a lot more dead and monstrous, that is. Again, I assume that it is because dhampirs experience things different from the Kindred, but in 2e they felt so much more.. alive, and I kinda miss that in that section.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;does he think he loves it&amp;quot;- yet another example of the lack of passion I miss so much.<br /> <br /> Yeah, yeah, having a dhampir is a bad idea... too much word count about why a vampire who makes dhampirs is an idiot, I think.<br /> <br /> general feeling until now is that the text has spend too much about saying why being a dhampir sucks. I want it to focus more about why being dhampir is awesome instead.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;guardian devil&amp;quot;. That's cool.<br /> <br /> Will we get something more substantial about all the &amp;quot;purpose&amp;quot; thingy, or is it just a RP thing?<br /> <br /> Haven't we already covered how vampires feels toward their children?<br /> <br /> Haven't we already covered how dhampirs act in the All Night Society in the same section?<br /> <br /> Really, up until now I personally don't really enjoy that section. I hope the next would be better.<br /> <br /> wait- so are there many dhampirs who work as hunters or aren't? It looks like each passage claims it to be otherwise...<br /> <br /> So dhampirs are the horror stories vampires tell each other when they go for camping in the mountains? Now, that's cool!<br /> <br /> I must say that considering the many hunter references, I'm surprised that Hunter didn't showed up in the Crossover section.<br /> <br /> The Boogeymen sound really cool. Now we are back on the track. I wonder if they could be styled as a compact/conspiracy<br /> <br /> So dhampirs can't make of their own kind. Then why did they kept it a mystery earlier? Anyway, the last section was much better written than the previous one, IMO.<br /> <br /> Well, that's not much, but I have homework in Quantum Mechanics to do, so I'll stop here before I'll start reviewing the Character Creation part. As this post was kinda more harsh than I usually make, feel free to disagree with everything I said :P</div> </div> </div> </div> I point out that with the Cruac the Dampyr's can in fact make more of their kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T09:20:13-08:00","id":1165068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165063#post1165063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I point out that with the Cruac the Dampyr's can in fact make more of their kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even the rar Dhampyr capable of learning Cruac, the circle would be hesitant about teaching that kind of ritual to.<br /> <br /> Would it even work for them, or a ghoul, even if they were taught it? <br /> <br /> oh curious?<br /> <br /> which works better Dhampyrs own fortune telling abilitys? or The Pool of Forbidden Truths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T09:22:57-08:00","id":1165070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165063#post1165063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I point out that with the Cruac the Dampyr's can in fact make more of their kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cruac solves everything! Oh. And for weird body horror? I'm sure there's a Cruac for making your dhampir daddy-momma into a real momma before you put something gestating inside them with your ritual of fecundity. Or not, if they're <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junior_(1994_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Schwarzenegger</a>. <br /> <br /> LostLight, you're not wrong: the Dhampir section especially from chapter 2 onward is, to be blunt, a mess. It's less than coherent, raises questions without answering them, and often provides contradictory information with itself or its themes. I would toss it back for a full, thoughtful edit and re-write, personally. Not sure if that will result from the errata thread but I hope so! <br /> <br /> Dhampirs also seem to incorporate more Masquerade themes than VtR, which is a weird and unpleasant off-note. It's not as bad as their portrayal in Wicked Dead, however.<br /> <br /> Look forward to the rest of your walk through the book.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T10:02:13-08:00","id":1165084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165070#post1165070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dhampirs also seem to incorporate more Masquerade themes than VtR, which is a weird and unpleasant off-note.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of get this vibe from the entire book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T11:25:14-08:00","id":1165098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165084#post1165084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of get this vibe from the entire book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. I think it's either a confusion on the part of the writers, or perhaps signals getting crossed when approaching the subject matter. Consider: all three sub-splats are mixed up with vampires in a way that creates widely disparate power dynamics. That is, in other words, the entire focus of Masquerade: that the Undead Man is keeping you down and you'll never, ever be respected because you're like, a kid, ya'know--so burn it all down!<br /> <br /> Tiresome '90s retread.<br /> <br /> I'm going to bite my tongue and let LostLight continue his Let's Read without dumping my opinions in a huge, steaming pile. Suffice to say I'll be particularly interested in his take.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:30:05-08:00","id":1165285,"title":"","content":"curious? what 'Lesser Rewards&quot;' Can a kindred offer a revenant working for them? before actualy offering to uplift them? <br /> <br /> <br /> Beyond the obvious of $$$$<br /> <br /> Which you can only offer if your affluent yourself.<br /> <br /> Discipline instruction is another not sure how kindred will feel about you teaching your clans signature discipline to a Revenant<br /> <br /> another thing? <br /> <br /> would it be that unlikely, for a ventrue to offer a Revenant who seemed a worthy kindred, but not a worth ventrue, a letter of reference to a appropiate sire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:09:48-08:00","id":1165295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165285#post1165285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">curious? what 'Lesser Rewards&quot;' Can a kindred offer a revenant working for them? before actualy offering to uplift them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Beyond the obvious of $$$$<br /> <br /> Which you can only offer if your affluent yourself.<br /> <br /> Discipline instruction is another not sure how kindred will feel about you teaching your clans signature discipline to a Revenant<br /> <br /> another thing?<br /> <br /> would it be that unlikely, for a ventrue to offer a Revenant who seemed a worthy kindred, but not a worth ventrue, a letter of reference to a appropiate sire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering that most revenants (and, for that matter most kindred) wouldn't even know that uplifting is a thing unless told... I would suppose what kindred could offer would be the usual:<br /> <br /> * Security/stability: a place to stay, a place to hunt/feed and attempt a semblance of human life. Considering revenant existence starts with &quot;OMG monster&quot; and resumes there every night? Stability is a VERY welcome offer!<br /> <br /> * Consistent blood supply: helping them arrange a herd that will be present when they wake is essential. That could mean animals, or blood dolls. The feeding thing is a huge time-sink and any help with that would be MOST attractive.<br /> <br /> * Money, sure. It can't buy you happiness, but it can buy out the pet store....<br /> <br /> * Discipline instruction would be pretty far down the list.<br /> <br /> * Uplifting (even the knowledge of uplifting) would be last. This would include introductions. Keep in mind that choosing to uplift is similar to choosing to embrace: costly in Humanity and favors to the Prince. That said, if the Prince is cool with the rev being around at all--putting extra feeding pressure on the city and generally acting like a Gangrel on bad behavior, then the Prince is probably going to look favorably on one of his vassals &quot;fixing&quot; the problem in a non-violent manner. Favors in, favors out.<br /> <br /> By the time the Rev is uplifted, he owes everything to virtually everyone.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:40:54-08:00","id":1165302,"title":"","content":"So how is this book? Is it useful for someone who does not use revenants and dhampir? Will it make me willing to use them? Is it set in &quot;woe is me&quot; and &quot;vampire bad because bad&quot; tone? How messy are the rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:30:07-08:00","id":1165318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165302#post1165302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it useful for someone who does not use revenants and dhampir?</div> </div> </div> </div>A third of the book is dedicated to ghouls, but unless you want to expand on the ghoul appendix in the core book it's not really useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will it make me willing to use them? </div> </div> </div>Maybe. The part about dhampirs brings mostly new stuff, but it's also the messiest of the three parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it set in &quot;woe is me&quot; and &quot;vampire bad because bad&quot; tone? </div> </div> </div>Yes. It'd be fine if it was one of several perspectives presented, but that's not the case here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How messy are the rules? </div> </div> </div>Not much at all. I think it's the best part of the book. And if we're lucky they might actually fix up some of the messier rules and not just focus on grammar/spelling when doing the final edit.<br /> Side note: I'm not personally a fan of the floaty Themes for dhampirs, but that's a matter of opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T09:47:11-08:00","id":1165343,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Dhampir 3- Character Creation</u></b><br /> <br /> Tam da da dam!<br /> <br /> yeah yeah, dhampirs are trapped between two sides like any child of a monster. Let's get to the good stuff.<br /> <br /> wait, you explicitly say that Hunter works well with dhampirs, but do not talk about them at all at the Crossover section? Again, missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> Again that &quot;created for a reason&quot; thing. I hope it would be backed mechanically. I must say, that when you consider the fact that from one side they were made for a reason, and from the other they have never meant to be, what you get is that by simply giving birth to a vampire you say &quot;SCREW YOU&quot; to all gods, all nature and fate itself. The Ordo Dracul should have explored that angle, IMO.<br /> <br /> I must say that all of that emphasis about fate and vampires reminds me of Kindred of the East's version of dhamps. I'll have to check it.<br /> <br /> I like how Destiny is presented- but does it meant to be the purpose behind the dhamp's birth, something assigned to them by some other higher power or something else? When I examined the strix in my blog, I related their version of Fate (or Doom) with the fate that people's heart and desires bring upon the world- or the product of your own inner darkness and to where does it lead you. Perhaps the dhamp's &quot;fate&quot; is also more of that style (that is, their own passion which twist reality to bring upon it their own doom).<br /> <br /> Omen Sensitivity and Thief of Fate. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> needless repetition.<br /> <br /> So the Beast does embody itself in its children. Nice.<br /> <br /> So dhampirs have Unseen Senses- Vampires? Why wasn't it mentioned before? Did I missed it?<br /> <br /> Wait- it is a general Unseen Sense and they can specifically recognize vamps? Does it also work on Wicked Dead?<br /> <br /> While I like crossover notes, it feels a bit like too many crossover notes.<br /> <br /> So Doom made a comeback! Yay! It also makes me think that the way I read their &quot;fate&quot; is, more or less, correct.<br /> <br /> Oh, here is the Unseen Sense section.<br /> <br /> So dhampirs want Vitae like vamps, can't take it from humans but only from vamps, and if they don't get it they... what? Will be very angry? I hope that the effects of not drinking Vitae would show up later, or I would ignore it.<br /> <br /> I've thought we are over that &quot;vampires are emotionally dead&quot; thing. It kinda feels like the writer haven't read 2e Core, which is kinda sad...<br /> <br /> Blood Sympathy for dhampires makes sense.<br /> <br /> I do like the Insomnia section, but it feels like they should have mentioned that dhamps suffer from a sleep deprivation Condition constantly.<br /> <br /> well, it's already late in here and I'm right before a very big section, so I'll continue next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:09:42-08:00","id":1165368,"title":"","content":"While RichT wants the errata thread to remain, well, errata. I hope we can cobble together a coherent list of ... um ... editorial oversights... yeah--and submit that. <br /> <br /> I'm making my own notes....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:10:04-08:00","id":1165399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165343#post1165343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that all of that emphasis about fate and vampires reminds me of Kindred of the East's version of dhamps. I'll have to check it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. IIRC, the KotE dhampirs are simply really lucky (which manifests in a few different ways) rather than their luck seemingly having a specific vector as it does here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like how Destiny is presented- but does it meant to be the purpose behind the dhamp's birth, something assigned to them by some other higher power or something else? </div> </div> </div>I got the impression of something assigned by &quot;fate,&quot; (in scarequotes, because I also get the impression that it's meant to come with a silent &quot;whatever the hell that means&quot;) which <i>might</i> at first coincide with the purpose behind their creation. The fact that you get a new destiny if you somehow fulfill your existing one would seem to rule out it having to be about why they were made.<br /> <br /> The interesting part is that it doesn't particularly seem to be tied to vampirism. It's suggested that creating a dhampir defies fate, so fate takes an interest, but that sounds less like an explanation than a way of pretending you don't need one. Back when it was first stated that the clans appeared independently - more like Promethean Lineages than Masquerade clans - I pointed out that the supernature that creates Lineages has an existence than manifests in a bunch of other ways too, and wondered if the same goes for the supernature of vampires. I wonder if dhampir fate-twisting is a case of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do like the Insomnia section, but it feels like they should have mentioned that dhamps suffer from a sleep deprivation Condition constantly. </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> I can't tell, but have you got as far as the personality kinks that derive from the clan bane of the vampire parent? I rather like those (in some cases more than the clan bane itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T14:25:47-08:00","id":1165425,"title":"","content":"Another issue, Eating flies, says that it will not let you actualy extract vitae from insects, but that it WILL let you gain vitae from every 2 &quot;Size 0 Creatures&quot; you feed on...<br /> <br /> what other then a Insect worm or arachnid has Size 0?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:56:08-08:00","id":1165450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165425#post1165425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue, Eating flies, says that it will not let you actualy extract vitae from insects, but that it WILL let you gain vitae from every 2 &amp;quot;Size 0 Creatures&amp;quot; you feed on...<br /> <br /> what other then a Insect worm or arachnid has Size 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Newborns from small rodent species? Even toads are Size 1 according to the animal stat blocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:16:25-08:00","id":1165456,"title":"","content":"It seems like 1st ed Changing Breeds. An excellent book to use the rules and create your own fluff, because the author was a nostalgic nut-job. At least we don't have bird titties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T18:26:55-08:00","id":1165484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165456#post1165456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like 1st ed Changing Breeds. An excellent book to use the rules and create your own fluff, because the author was a nostalgic nut-job. At least we don't have bird titties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! Knock that the fuck off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T19:37:02-08:00","id":1165500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165456#post1165456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like 1st ed Changing Breeds. An excellent book to use the rules and create your own fluff, because the author was a nostalgic nut-job. At least we don't have bird titties.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>This is a personal attack against the author.</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rule 1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t personally attack other users, members of their gaming groups, and so on. Also, don\u2019t attack groups of people. That means avoiding racist, sexist, homophobic, transphobic and similar insults. Racial, sexual, and other slurs, as well as misgendering, count as insults. Please also avoid broad declarations that attack a group of people to get around making a \u201cpersonal\u201d attack. Like all rules, this rule applies equally to people working for Onyx Path, White Wolf, Paradox, and CCP.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T12:53:10-08:00","id":1165644,"title":"","content":"And the cover art is lame, of course it's lame, I wonder if Onyx Path would listen if I start a petition for changing the art style of future source books<br /> <br /> Why can't we have more books with the art direction and quality of New Wave Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T15:40:18-08:00","id":1165687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165644#post1165644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the cover art is lame, of course it's lame, I wonder if Onyx Path would listen if I start a petition for changing the art style of future source books<br /> <br /> Why can't we have more books with the art direction and quality of New Wave Requiem?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Lame&quot; isn't much of constructive criticism, you know that right? What's wrong with the cover though? I find it pretty appealing and evocative with a aura of symbolism and metaphor.<br /> Can't really agree on the NWR though, except for the Cover art, which is awesome. The rest is way to comic-book stylish for my taste, a trend that was in the end of 1st ed requiem when they started with the full colour in the books. Myself is thankful that era has ended. I'm not saying the 2ed art is great all the times, but overall it's way better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T15:44:25-08:00","id":1165689,"title":"","content":"I like the cover art. I adore the cover art for NWR, but I think the cover art for Half-Damned is decent.<br /> <br /> Really not a fan of most of the art <i>in</i> the book, but there are a couple good pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T16:36:51-08:00","id":1165701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165687#post1165687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Lame&amp;quot; isn't much of constructive criticism, you know that right? What's wrong with the cover though? I find it pretty appealing and evocative with a aura of symbolism and metaphor.<br /> Can't really agree on the NWR though, except for the Cover art, which is awesome. The rest is way to comic-book stylish for my taste, a trend that was in the end of 1st ed requiem when they started with the full colour in the books. Myself is thankful that era has ended. I'm not saying the 2ed art is great all the times, but overall it's way better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using &quot;lame&quot; to mean stupid is also derogatory in the exact same way that using &quot;gay&quot; or &quot;retarded&quot; as an insult is, society only just starting to realize it now. It is a word worth expunging from your vocabulary.<br /> <br /> Above and beyond that, chalk me up as another person who likes the cover art. It's moody and it gets the point across of vampires hovering around in the background of the half-damned's lives, guidinf and controlling them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T16:38:20-08:00","id":1165702,"title":"","content":"I have the poster for the cover of New Wave Requiem.<br /> <br /> But it's a vampiress in skimpy clothes, so it's an easy sell.<br /> <br /> Love Sam Araya's art, I wouldn't ever insult it, though I think the cover would be better showing a dhampir, revenant and ghoul. But I've simple tastes when it comes to art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Second Chances was right 12-06-2017, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T16:56:07-08:00","id":1165705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165701#post1165701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using &quot;lame&quot; to mean stupid is also derogatory in the exact same way that using &quot;gay&quot; or &quot;retarded&quot; as an insult is, society only just starting to realize it now. It is a word worth expunging from your vocabulary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agree on this one! Didn't want to call it out though as I didn't want it to be interpreted as Hobby-moderating as well as fueling the flame.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T18:05:34-08:00","id":1165717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165701#post1165701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using &quot;lame&quot; to mean stupid is also derogatory in the exact same way that using &quot;gay&quot; or &quot;retarded&quot; as an insult is, society only just starting to realize it now. It is a word worth expunging from your vocabulary.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a physically-disabled person I'd like to politely disagree: &quot;Gay&quot; and &quot;retarded&quot; are still regularly used to demean the groups of people they refer to, while at this point &quot;lame&quot; tends to only mean &quot;uncool&quot;, and I don't think I've ever seen it used to attack people with walking difficulties (i.e. the literal meaning of the word), which at this point is outright archaic. In general, this is <i>a good thing</i>, as it means the word has entirely lost its sting, and bringing up its ableist origins like this may be empowering it to harm again.<br /> <br /> I realize this is just one person's view, but as a member of the group in question, I'd really prefer people not try to make &quot;lame&quot; genuinely ableist again, even if the intention is well-meaning (i.e. to get people to stop using it). I'd rather not empower the word to be used as a slur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:06:15-08:00","id":1165841,"title":"","content":"I'd rather not see insults directed at artists and writers on these or any other forum.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'd rather not see insults directed at all. (And yes, I try and often fail to keep my own snark colored within the lines.)<br /> <br /> VtR is one product of a busy setting of major splats. We're posting here because vamps and their world interest us, and care about the books that come out for VtR because there are relatively few, precious spots to put Onyx Path-sanctioned material into circulation. We'd like it to be &quot;right&quot;, high-quality, and up the game. That puts people on edge. Still, there is no excuse for rudeness.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> I am sorry your thread has been shat upon.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:36:03-08:00","id":1165888,"title":"","content":"It's ok, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>- and you are right. We should return to focus around making a review as clean as possible. It is ok to not like some of the material and to criticize it, but let's maintain a polite and respectful discussion.<br /> <br /> Anyway- <br /> <br /> <b><u>Dhampir 4- Kewel Powerz!</u></b><br /> <br /> So cursed children have curse powers. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Well, Twists sound flexible- I wonder if that's truly the case.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they are flexible- somewhat more like the variant Blood Sorcery system than Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Twists could be seen as the dhampir embodying their Destiny into reality, with the dhampirs themselves being the desire of their parent embodied in a child- or perhaps, their parent's Doom. Yeah, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> The Daeva's Twist makes sense- the Daeva is used to be at the center of attention, the dhampir force her to care only about him. Sounds like a legit &quot;clan doom&quot;.<br /> <br /> Desire and Submission are written much better than Attention, IMO<br /> <br /> The Gangrel are the perfect predators, their dhampirs are the most malleable prey. Good luck biting something that flows between your teeth.<br /> <br /> I have some problem with Twists and Themes as they don't really feel like supernatural powers- but it makes sense, as they are subtle kind of powers.<br /> <br /> Ooooooh the Mekhet's Twist is cool! Also, giving a liar's ability to a Clan which works hard to discover the truth under the surface makes great &quot;doom&quot; to them.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu are forced into being ugly, their spawn choose it.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are kings by right and duty, their children steal their crown and throw it to the garbage when they need it no more.<br /> <br /> As for the Twists themselves-<br /> <br /> 1 Dot-<br /> Dissent makes sense. Bestial Echo isn't really fate-like, but they are vampire children after all. Karma is fine. Foreboding is awesome.<br /> <br /> 2 Dots-<br /> Fate's Call makes sense. Draught of Power- finally, a reason to actually drink Vitae! Defiance makes sense. I like Sibyl's Curse. Portent sounds fine. Fortuity is standard considering the situation.<br /> <br /> 3 Dots-<br /> Intuition's Call makes sense. Insurgence shouldn't have been a separate power. Oooooh I do like Doubling Down! Heir's Draught- yet another reason to drink Vitae!<br /> <br /> Blood Magic for dhamps? Sounds nice.<br /> <br /> Wait- THE Blood Magic which eventually evolved to Curac? I've thought that Curac was the outcome of a number of Blood Sorceries being melded together into a mish mash of blood and terror. I assume that it is a reference to Veneficia, but the Gauls had their own Blood Magic at the time which was presented as Curac- so in sort, Curac is both new and ancient. Nothing serious, but it just sting my eye a bit.<br /> <br /> Ah- so it is about Malisons, not &quot;Curac for dhamps&quot;. Oh well.<br /> <br /> Again, the &quot;Beast Embody itself in children&quot; theory sounds more and more reasonable.<br /> <br /> Blood Curses- there is nothing uncool in Blood Curses.<br /> <br /> So the &quot;Blood&quot; is treated as a real entity? Something to consider.<br /> <br /> Wait- &quot;very rarely are there two dhampirs in the same place in the same time&quot;? What about the Boogeymen? You know, that vampire hunter group which is made from those half damned?<br /> <br /> For the Malisons themselves-<br /> <br /> I like Blood Oath. Haruspicy sounds veeeeeery Veneficia. Katabasis is interesting. Nemesis is great. Pallor of Death is interesting. Wait- so that witch from Game of Thrones is a dhampir with Shadow Play? Because it sounds like it. Anyway- awesome, and I wonder if it could be used against the strix in some way. Wrack and Ruin sounds great. Ooooh Unmasking fucks you so hard that its awesome!<br /> <br /> Afflictions- I think they should have appeared earlier in the book, as they are much more basic in nature than Twists and Malisons.<br /> <br /> So dhampirs are once again referred as the products of Blood Magic. Is it me, or that it feels like there were two writers for this chapter, and there were some communication problems between them?<br /> <br /> Strix have Vices. Humans have Vices. Strix are a type of Beasts. Dhampirs have two Vices. What does it tell you?<br /> <br /> Also, was it said before that they get two Vices and I missed/forgot it? If not, that that section really should have been earlier in this sub-chapter.<br /> <br /> The Daeva become addicted to their followers, their dhampirs break their connection with their followers. Nice foil.<br /> <br /> Gangrel run with the Beast, their children are overtaken by it.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet are bound by secrets, their kids are bound to sniff them out.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu are cursed by loneliness, their spawn choose it.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are detached from the folk, their heirs are compelled to actively rule them.<br /> <br /> Time for Merits-<br /> <br /> Beloved Stranger- because not all dhampirs had such a fucked up life. Blood Dissonance- cool. Hand of Doom- awesome. Mother's Army Recruit makes sense. Night's Child- because you can even a decent child even among the dead. Omen Sensitivity- we really had to have this merit reprinted? Requiem Counterpoint is nice. Thief of Fate- see Omen Sensitivity. Vampire Hunter- because it had to be a thing. <br /> <br /> Well, I still have a weekly blog post to finish and things to do, so we'll stop here. Yes, this was a good sub-chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T10:14:48-08:00","id":1165891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165888#post1165888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Afflictions- I think they should have appeared earlier in the book, as they are much more basic in nature than Twists and Malisons.<br /> <br /> So dhampirs are once again referred as the products of Blood Magic. Is it me, or that it feels like there were two writers for this chapter, and there were some communication problems between them?<br /> <br /> Strix have Vices. Humans have Vices. Strix are a type of Beasts. Dhampirs have two Vices. What does it tell you?<br /> <br /> Also, was it said before that they get two Vices and I missed/forgot it? If not, that that section really should have been earlier in this sub-chapter.<br /> <br /> Time for Merits-<br /> <br /> Beloved Stranger- because not all dhampirs had such a fucked up life. Blood Dissonance- cool. Hand of Doom- awesome. Mother's Army Recruit makes sense. Night's Child- because you can even a decent child even among the dead. Omen Sensitivity- we really had to have this merit reprinted? Requiem Counterpoint is nice. Thief of Fate- see Omen Sensitivity. Vampire Hunter- because it had to be a thing.<br /> <br /> Well, I still have a weekly blog post to finish and things to do, so we'll stop here. Yes, this was a good sub-chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most appreciate the point, LostLight, that the clan affiliations for dhampir are essentially mirror foils of their parents. <br /> <br /> Most of the book seems like it was touched by several writers, who didn't always read what the other was writing. There is much redundancy and inconsistency.<br /> <br /> Dhampir only enjoy a second Vice when they use their last point of willpower to fuel a Twist, or take damage in their rightmost 3 boxes to fuel a Malison. These are pretty edge cases, I think--certainly desperate! At that point, then, the dhampir enjoys the Affliction vices. It's a little unfortunate, as some of the Afflictions are pretty cool!<br /> <br /> Beloved Stranger is, alone, enough to make the best F'ing friend to the Prince. Rock on, wayward son!<br /> <br /> Note: Thief of Fate is all &quot;drawback&quot;. I think that is an errata-level error.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:35:51-08:00","id":1165931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165888#post1165888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some problem with Twists and Themes as they don't really feel like supernatural powers- but it makes sense, as they are subtle kind of powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found their write-up very hard to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:50:36-08:00","id":1165939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165931#post1165931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found their write-up very hard to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, it takes awhile to digest the writeup and understand how exactly to Twists and Themes work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:52:48-08:00","id":1165940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165701#post1165701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using &amp;quot;lame&amp;quot; to mean stupid is also derogatory in the exact same way that using &amp;quot;gay&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;retarded&amp;quot; as an insult is, society only just starting to realize it now. It is a word worth expunging from your vocabulary.<br /> <br /> Above and beyond that, chalk me up as another person who likes the cover art. It's moody and it gets the point across of vampires hovering around in the background of the half-damned's lives, guidinf and controlling them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize if the words I used were offensive, it wasn't my intent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T15:39:59-08:00","id":1165961,"title":"","content":"It was also a bit rude. There's nicer ways to state one's opinion than saying that something suck.<br /> <br /> I like the cover. It doesn't really convey what the book's about, but that might be difficult in this case. At least they made a good attempt after the extremely nondescript cover of Thousand Years of Night.<br /> As for the art inside the book; nothing was really breathtaking, but most of it was still interesting. While the quality wasn't always great from a purely technical standpoint (page 40 being somewhat unintentionally hilarious), almost all of the images had some action or details that told a story about what they depicted, or were otherwise evocative. Only the ghoul chapter suffered from boring depictions of ghouls doing generic tasks for their regnants. That and the full page illustration on page 48, but I tend not to see the full page illustrations as I only use PDFs and navigate primarily through bookmarks or learned page numbers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>: I've like your reports thus far, but there's a little thing that irks me. You've consistently written Curac instead of Cr\u00faac, and while it's not the end of the world I just couldn't not point it out any longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-07-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T15:57:41-08:00","id":1165965,"title":"","content":"So, how about those revenants. That's the next chapter, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T22:44:45-08:00","id":1166023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165961#post1165961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">earned page numbers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>: I've like your reports thus far, but there's a little thing that irks me. You've consistently written Curac instead of Cr\u00faac, and while it's not the end of the world I just couldn't not point it out any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I do have some words which I make such mistakes (it took me awhile to stop writing &quot;Exrach&quot; instead of Exarch, for example). Noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how about those revenants. That's the next chapter, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost. There is one more section in the dhampir chapter, and then I'll more to revenants. I try to not read ahead of time in order to document my reaction to the book in real time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T09:29:04-08:00","id":1166111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165961#post1165961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was also a bit rude. There's nicer ways to state one's opinion than saying that something suck.<br /> <br /> I like the cover. It doesn't really convey what the book's about, but that might be difficult in this case. At least they made a good attempt after the extremely nondescript cover of Thousand Years of Night.<br /> As for the art inside the book; nothing was really breathtaking, but most of it was still interesting. While the quality wasn't always great from a purely technical standpoint (page 40 being somewhat unintentionally hilarious), almost all of the images had some action or details that told a story about what they depicted, or were otherwise evocative. Only the ghoul chapter suffered from boring depictions of ghouls doing generic tasks for their regnants. That and the full page illustration on page 48, but I tend not to see the full page illustrations as I only use PDFs and navigate primarily through bookmarks or learned page numbers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>: I've like your reports thus far, but there's a little thing that irks me. You've consistently written Curac instead of Cr\u00faac, and while it's not the end of the world I just couldn't not point it out any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How much of the english language must be sacraficed on the Altar of politeness? <br /> <br /> I'm frail, but wont be offended if you call an idea lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:01:39-08:00","id":1166116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166111#post1166111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of the english language must be sacraficed on the Altar of politeness?<br /> <br /> I'm frail, but wont be offended if you call an idea lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have already pointed out the choice of words was unfortunate for more reasons than just impoliteness.<br /> The reason I pointed out that it was also rude is because it's straddling the line between just a stated opinion (&quot;I don't like this&quot;) and an attack against the artists/art direction (&quot;this is shit&quot;). It's a minor thing and I probably wouldn't have cared most other times, but there is also the context of the user having previously banned for a week for insulting VtR artists as well as other repeat offences. (Edit: In hindsight this might've been hobby moderation and I probably should've just reported the post.)<br /> <br /> Compare with me, who haven't been holding back on my criticism about Half-Damned in another thread, but I've also presented it as an opinion piece, and tried to give some constructive criticism towards the next VtR supplement. When I realised it could've been construed as a personal attack (a dev managed to post right before me, and my intention was to address the devs in general) I went back to edit my post and even messaged the dev to explain that it wasn't supposed to be directed to them personally.<br /> <br /> Now, you might not react to people being rude about something you've spent a lot of time creating, but that doesn't really mean it's okay to do so. I know how extremely discouraging such &quot;criticism&quot; can be and it's not a good thing. Certainly not towards the creator, but also not for anyone who's interested in further products because if such remarks have any effect on future products it's most likely a negative one as the affected creator has less enthusiasm about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-08-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T02:16:36-08:00","id":1166257,"title":"","content":"so let's return to subject, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Dhampir- last post!</u></b><br /> <br /> The &quot;dhampirs as NPCs section&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs- the incarnated doom of their parents.<br /> <br /> Wait- Final Demise? I think that's an errata stuff. Was it mentioned in the thread?<br /> <br /> Yeah, dhampirs do make good antagonists.<br /> <br /> The regular &quot;don't abuse your players&quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Actually, it looks like that section is quit good- much better than some other sections in that chapter.<br /> <br /> I'm really disappointed that there isn't some extra material about the Boogeymen- like example characters and such.<br /> <br /> Again, hunter-dhampir crossover. Just make the Boogeymen a conspiracy already :P<br /> <br /> Really, too much of crossover in a vampire book.<br /> <br /> Seriously- all that crossover talk and Beast got only one line?<br /> <br /> I really thing that the position of the dhampirs as prophets and readers of omens should have taken a much greater place when elaborating their place in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Also- where are the strix? I want to know how the Owls react to half bloods- and heck, what would happen if an Owl possessed vampire would sire a child?<br /> <br /> Ala- oh, I like that. The choice of name was very in theme. Is it me, or that the ale feel a bit like &quot;strix possessed&quot;, with all of that &quot;black shadow of doom&quot; thing? Again, maybe inside each dhampir there is a small strix waiting to hatch.<br /> <br /> Oh, the writeup has already established a strix- ale connection. Finally. Yeeeeeeeeesssssssssss.<br /> <br /> I would have preferred to get an actual writeup of an ala together with certain Dread Power suggestions instead of just sending me to the CofD rulebook. I would simply give them access to Strix Doom Powers, together with Shadow Potency and the ability to drink Vitae, but with a degrading Integrity up into the level they turn into a living incarnation of Doom.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many of the Boogeymen are actually Ale.<br /> <br /> I like the wide range of possibilities presented for the use of dhamps.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Chapter Sum Up!</u></b><br /> <br /> <u><b>The Good</b></u><br /> <br /> - playable dhamps.<br /> <br /> - tie in for Hunter crossover<br /> <br /> - the CotC, the Invictus and the Ordo's views.<br /> <br /> - the Half Blood Director<br /> <br /> - Boogeymen and ale<br /> <br /> - Doom and Insomaina<br /> <br /> - Afflictions as foils and mini Beasts<br /> <br /> - Twists and Malisons<br /> <br /> - Beloved Stranger, Night Child and Hand of Doom<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Bad</u></b><br /> <br /> - a major lack of consistency, to the point it becomes confusing. <br /> <br /> - the &quot;vampire demonization&quot;<br /> <br /> - not enough strix<br /> <br /> - not having mentions of Beast and Hunter in the Crossover section. Also, too many crossover references.<br /> <br /> - the contradiction between the Lance's presented view and the Testament.<br /> <br /> - not having stats for Boogeymen and ale.<br /> <br /> - some missed opportunities.<br /> <br /> - needless repetitions.<br /> <br /> - some problems with the book's structure.<br /> <br /> - lacking the disadvantages of Blood Lust and Insomania<br /> <br /> - the unclear way Themes were written<br /> <br /> In sort, there is both good and bad in this chapter, more or less equally- the problem is that the &quot;good&quot; is very concentrated and the the &quot;bad&quot; is all over the place, which sometimes could make you grind your teeth. While it is clear that the writers has put a lot of work into the book, it felt like there was some misuse of word-count, which is more of the editor/developer's work than the writers. The main complain is that the chapter was messy, and that it was full of contradictions- but there are some really good gems in there, which should have been polished better so they could shine stronger. Also, while I understand the reason for the &quot;vampire demonization&quot;, I think it was a bit over the edge and should have been toned down- after all, those who buy the book are Requiem fans, not Hunter/Masquerade, and it should have been taken into account, I think.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Commercials, once more- Fiction!</u></b><br /> The hell did I just read? That wasn't a pleasant fiction. I can't say it made me want to play a revenant. Yikes. Yeah, I know it is an horror game- but I have a very refined taste for horror, and that was a bit too much. I also didn't really liked the writing style- but all of this is a personal flavor, so I assume other people would have other preferences. <br /> <br /> Next time- starting the revenant chapter!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T13:41:07-08:00","id":1166330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sparketh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165500#post1165500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>This is a personal attack against the author.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't noticed it at the time, sorry, my bad. Should I edit the post? I'm sincerely not sure.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165717#post1165717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a physically-disabled person I'd like to politely disagree: &quot;Gay&quot; and &quot;retarded&quot; are still regularly used to demean the groups of people they refer to, while at this point &quot;lame&quot; tends to only mean &quot;uncool&quot;, and I don't think I've ever seen it used to attack people with walking difficulties (i.e. the literal meaning of the word), which at this point is outright archaic. In general, this is <i>a good thing</i>, as it means the word has entirely lost its sting, and bringing up its ableist origins like this may be empowering it to harm again.<br /> <br /> I realize this is just one person's view, but as a member of the group in question, I'd really prefer people not try to make &quot;lame&quot; genuinely ableist again, even if the intention is well-meaning (i.e. to get people to stop using it). I'd rather not empower the word to be used as a slur.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I second that. As much as &quot;lame&quot; does have a rather derogatory meaning, it isn't linked to disabled people anymore in its use. As a mentally-disabled person I already saw too much what the well-meaning of &quot;non-affected&quot; people can do. As our motto says, &quot;nothing about us without us&quot;.<br /> <br /> But regardless, I'm seeing too much of those heated discussions about the art of the books nowadays here. I'm not a fan of most of the style used today, though I find it better than the start of the First edition. But it is pretty much a question of taste first and foremost. It is relevant, sure, and we can discuss it in the manner of how the art delivers the mood of the book. Personally, I find it hard to dislike so much this art considering my personal opinion for WtA's covers and most of its internal art.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165841#post1165841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather not see insults directed at artists and writers on these or any other forum.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'd rather not see insults directed at all. (And yes, I try and often fail to keep my own snark colored within the lines.)<br /> <br /> VtR is one product of a busy setting of major splats. We're posting here because vamps and their world interest us, and care about the books that come out for VtR because there are relatively few, precious spots to put Onyx Path-sanctioned material into circulation. We'd like it to be &quot;right&quot;, high-quality, and up the game. That puts people on edge. Still, there is no excuse for rudeness.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> I am sorry your thread has been shat upon.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. I didn't thought through what I was posting, and sometimes I get confused with what is or is not a proper comment. It took me several minutes to understand what I did.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166111#post1166111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of the english language must be sacraficed on the Altar of politeness?<br /> <br /> I'm frail, but wont be offended if you call an idea lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of it and all of it. The discussion itself is the good point, it meaning that the question became relevant instead of invisible. With a hard-to-notice disability, I can say how it hurts to be a invisible issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166257#post1166257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Chapter Sum Up!</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Overall it made me even more eager to get this book. I'll have to wait until the 20th to buy it, though. As it seems, it was a not-so-well edited good material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T15:20:57-08:00","id":1166345,"title":"","content":"One reason I think the dhampir is so &quot;messy&quot; is that this is, as far as I know, the most in-depth and lengthy attention they've gotten in <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i>, right? In Second Ed., certainly. So we're basically looking at the same thing the Kindred themselves were, waaaaayyyy back at the beginning, before all the books and editions and errata and reboots that polished and honed them into the pretty consistent and tight concept we have now. Dhampir are still the rough gem, sparkly but coarse, waiting to get cut into a jewel that can sit proudly on <i>VtR</i>'s greater necklace of ideas. Or something. It may not be all that comforting to those who'd like playable, tightly written dhampir <i>right now</i>, but it's worth bearing in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T15:46:00-08:00","id":1166351,"title":"","content":"My guess, on the messiness and possibly Masquerade feel of the thing, is that we kinda do have a new team. Rose has moved over to changeling, so we basically have a new vampire team. Much like there was a massive shift in Requiem's direction when Requiem for Rome came out, I think we're seeing a bit of confusion and finding-of-feet that the new group is having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T15:46:25-08:00","id":1166352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166330#post1166330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I second that. As much as &quot;lame&quot; does have a rather derogatory meaning, it isn't linked to disabled people anymore in its use. As a mentally-disabled person I already saw too much what the well-meaning of &quot;non-affected&quot; people can do. As our motto says, &quot;nothing about us without us&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to get into a debate about this, because the position is a valid, but I will clarify this: I live in the same sort boat that you do. There is a reason react to the word &quot;retard&quot; with blistering fury and my reaction to the word &quot;lame&quot; when it is used as dumb is largely a sympathetic reaction based off of that. If you have a disagreement with me on either of those words, I will absolutely listen. But politely, please don't assume that I am some well-meaning but cisabled person doesn't know what they are talking about. I've travelled that road too. <br /> <br /> All of this is off topic though, so let's drop it. <br /> <br /> I am a REALLY big fan of how Twists work for the Dhampir. I love Mage-like magic systems that allow for some creativity and flexibility. Blood &amp; Sacraments is also one of my books though, so this is no real surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-10-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T08:46:26-08:00","id":1166718,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Chapter 2- Revenants</u></b><br /> THE NIGHT OF THE LIVING DEAD BEGINS!!!<br /> <br /> Dante's Inferno quote. That's raaaaaaaad.<br /> <br /> Once against capital Blood as entity. So it's official? The Blood is Requiem's Wyrd/Principle/God Machine? I'll have to work it to my cosmology.<br /> <br /> Well, I must say I do like the opening paragraph. I really does make you think that revenants has always been in Requiem, unlike dhampir.<br /> <br /> &quot;Embrace of long lost clans whose blood runs as thin as water&quot;- that's awesome. &quot;From Revenant you came and to Revenant you shall return&quot; kind of thing. As &quot;blood thinning&quot; is not a Requiem thing, I wonder what cause a clan to lose its ability to Embrace- for the Utukku it is said to come from the destruction of Ur, so perhaps just as every clan rose on its own, their fall also come the same way? And if so, would it be possible to kill a clan in the same way?<br /> <br /> So this is how I see the &quot;Kindred Evolution&quot; path-<br /> <br /> Revenant --&gt; Wicked Dead --&gt; Kindred --&gt; Revenant<br /> <br /> company of outcasts kind of things. I like that.<br /> <br /> A monster child? Joseph, is that you? (Mahoutsukai no Yome reference)<br /> <br /> <i>.....Cartaphilus.....</i><br /> <br /> Well, that's a scary priestess.<br /> <br /> I must say that while it was a cool origin story- I'm not sure why revenants need such story. It would make much more sense for those half damned to rise before the Kindred, not after them. Saying &quot;revenants have been around since humanity, the hungry dead from which the first of the clans rose&quot; would make much more sense, IMO- but I assume that the revenants need something to tell themselves in order to sleep well at day.<br /> <br /> The &quot;we have our own laws in here&quot; is just awesome. Makes me think about that Neglatu prince in Egypt.<br /> <br /> So revenants are above ghouls even though the ghoul state is more &quot;complete&quot; than revenant's? (learning devotions and such). You, sir, are a hypocrite.<br /> <br /> Well, being a revenant sucks, I see.<br /> <br /> Number one law in the All Night Society- don't go kill people. You will end up dead. And if you do, make sure there is no body left behind. The same is still valid for revenants.<br /> <br /> I must say that this chapter manage to to deliver the messy relationships between revenants and Kindred much better than the dhampir one, without making vampires into lifeless monsters who are empty inside.<br /> <br /> I must say that I don't really like how the &quot;opening italic paragraph&quot; doesn't really corresponds to the following text. It also happened in the dhampir chapter. Again, editorial problem, not writer one.<br /> <br /> I can't understand the flow of text- one moment they talk about being a revenant, and then they start talking about the Mikhaili, with an italic section in the middle. It feels like a big editor oversight.<br /> <br /> In general, I find the Mikhaili story cool- I love the lost clans section. Also, is it me or that the text mentions that the last Mikhaili created a new Clan? The only weird thing is the thinning of blood, but I remember that it was said it is not really how things work.<br /> <br /> I wonder what would make a revenant to <i>not</i> want the Uplifting. Sure, freedom is nice and all- but it is the price you need to pay for stop having a <i>murder house</i> (also, it is cheaper than maintaining the said murder house).<br /> <br /> &quot;pity is a thing even dead hearts can feel&quot;- see, that's much more of a Requiem thing to say.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Childer of Church&quot; sounds really awesome kind of thing, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Now, while I do like the Mikhaili, there are two complains about them. Well, make it three, even though the third was a &quot;spoiler&quot;. First, their name feels way to mundane when compared to other clans, but I like how it rolls on the tongue so I can let it slide. Second, their Bane is much too paralyzing, and it does not based upon Humanity- again, I can let the last part slide as both the Jiang Shi and the Akhud's Banes are not Humanity based (even though I've homebrewed the last one), but perhaps by tying it to humanity the Mikhaili would be more playable and not practically dead for half a year. The last complain is that their Discipline, as presented, gives almost nothing for vampires- and it is a shame that the writer didn't manage to add their own version to the book.<br /> <br /> Well, that's it for now. I'm going to play Pokemon Go (gen 3 is out. Yay). See you next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-11-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T09:31:42-08:00","id":1166729,"title":"","content":"The Daeva clan bane isn't based on Humanity either. Its drink twice from the same person, fake-fall-in-love with them at any humanity level. Did you house rule that too? Curious minds inquiring.<br /> <br /> The vampire version of that discipline was also mentioned in the other Half-Damned thread. Its different abilities, close but not quite, if you want to check that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T10:17:18-08:00","id":1166745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166729#post1166729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva clan bane isn't based on Humanity either. Its drink twice from the same person, fake-fall-in-love with them at any humanity level. Did you house rule that too? Curious minds inquiring.<br /> <br /> The vampire version of that discipline was also mentioned in the other Half-Damned thread. Its different abilities, close but not quite, if you want to check that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider the Humanity roll as being &quot;Humanity based&quot;. As long as Humanity is involved some way or another, I'm satisfied. <br /> <br /> And yeah, I know the writer shared their notes on the Discipline- I'm just disappointed it wasn't in the finale book. If you want, you could put here a link to the post, so if someone who reads the thread would want to refer to it, they could easily do so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T11:54:14-08:00","id":1166758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166718#post1166718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I find the Mikhaili story cool- I love the lost clans section. Also, is it me or that the text mentions that the last Mikhaili created a new Clan? The only weird thing is the thinning of blood, but I remember that it was said it is not really how things work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I got was that they kind of used themselves up in their rush of embraces and started producing revenants, and then Gangrel diablerised them all. But every so often, when a Gangrel makes a revenant instead of a Kindred, that revenant carries a little echo of the Mikhaili.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:59:14-08:00","id":1166805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166729#post1166729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva clan bane isn't based on Humanity either. Its drink twice from the same person, fake-fall-in-love with them at any humanity level. Did you house rule that too? Curious minds inquiring.<br /> <br /> The vampire version of that discipline was also mentioned in the other Half-Damned thread. Its different abilities, close but not quite, if you want to check that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still doesn't kick in until you drop to humanity 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T14:35:04-08:00","id":1166820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166745#post1166745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider the Humanity roll as being &quot;Humanity based&quot;. As long as Humanity is involved some way or another, I'm satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humanity... roll? To drop to humanity 6? That's the only roll I see? I am confused. The Mik would get that same degeneration roll before the weakness kicked in, no? Am I missing something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T14:38:12-08:00","id":1166821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166820#post1166820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Humanity... roll? To drop to humanity 6? That's the only roll I see? I am confused. The Mik would get that same degeneration roll before the weakness kicked in, no? Am I missing something here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Daeva bane is &quot;roll your Humanity to avoid getting the Dependent Condition for a mortal character each time you drink from them beyond the first time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T14:54:10-08:00","id":1166828,"title":"","content":"Core book, page 103, second paragraph after the &quot;Clan Banes&quot; heading.<br /> <br /> Clan banes do not affect a vampire until she reaches six dots of Humanity. They do not go away if she regains her seventh dot; they remain with her throughout the rest of her Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T15:05:31-08:00","id":1166832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166821#post1166821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva bane is &quot;roll your Humanity to avoid getting the Dependent Condition for a mortal character each time you drink from them beyond the first time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird. My book doesn't have that. The book seems to be the latest one .... I'm going to download a fresh copy anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T15:26:58-08:00","id":1166839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166832#post1166832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird. My book doesn't have that. The book seems to be the latest one .... I'm going to download a fresh copy anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in my pre- and post-errata copies of Blood &amp; Smoke as well as my copy of Second Edition, and the only other place I can think of that the clan bane would be reproduced in the text is in the same abbreviated form every other clan writeup presents its bane in. &quot;Roll Humanity&quot; is in the middle of the block paragraph on page 103 where the clan banes are all collected, so it might have just slipped past recognition there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T16:14:41-08:00","id":1166853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166718#post1166718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I find the Mikhaili story cool- I love the lost clans section. Also, is it me or that the text mentions that the last Mikhaili created a new Clan? The only weird thing is the thinning of blood, but I remember that it was said it is not really how things work.<br /> ...<br /> Now, while I do like the Mikhaili, there are two complains about them. Well, make it three, even though the third was a &quot;spoiler&quot;. First, their name feels way to mundane when compared to other clans, but I like how it rolls on the tongue so I can let it slide. Second, their Bane is much too paralyzing, and it does not based upon Humanity- again, I can let the last part slide as both the Jiang Shi and the Akhud's Banes are not Humanity based (even though I've homebrewed the last one), but perhaps by tying it to humanity the Mikhaili would be more playable and not practically dead for half a year. The last complain is that their Discipline, as presented, gives almost nothing for vampires- and it is a shame that the writer didn't manage to add their own version to the book</div> </div> </div> </div>The Winter Kings are probably my favorite thing to come out of <i>Half-Damned</i>, though I'll admit I'm a huge sucker for lost clans. I also noticed the bit about the last Mikhaili creating a new clan, and the total absence of a follow-up. I wonder whether that's intentionally vague, to tease something in an upcoming book (<i>Spilled Blood</i>, perhaps?), or whether it is just an oversight tying into something that got left on the cutting-room floor.<br /> <br /> I actually really love the whole &quot;thin blood&quot; concept and how it ties into the Winter Kings' rise and fall. They start off with &quot;thick&quot; blood, that makes them powerful and curses them to slumber half the year. When they try to resist the Gangrel advance by mass Embrace, their blood &quot;thins&quot; to the point where they become much weaker individually and lose the power to create more non-revenant childer entirely. Of course, the text explicitly points out that the Blood doesn't work that way, but the story is also one that the Kindred have passed down, so it's almost certainly not an entirely accurate portrait of what happened. (more of a morality tale, &quot;don't Embrace too much or you'll dilute the clan's power&quot;)<br /> <br /> Even their banes follow this arc- the first one says that their thick, wintry blood forces them to hibernate half the year. I'd imagine that they lost this bane after a while, as their blood thinned and they gained the new bane, the one that prevents them from reproducing reliably. Interestingly, they both point to why the clan would struggle to survive in the Modern Nights; it's hard to hold territory reliably if you spend so much time helpless, and you're going to quickly be out-competed as a species if you can't actually reproduce. Survival of the fittest!<br /> <br /> I actually wonder if the whole thick/thin blood thing was a unique aspect of the Mikhaili's particular strain of the Curse. Like a quirk of evolution that allowed made them stronger than average as long as they didn't spread it out too much, but once the concentration was too low it became irreparable. Much like how the Jiang Shi have aspects that are unique to them while also sharing similarities to &quot;true&quot; Kindred. (their unique Embrace, the ability to return to their graves, how they have the Kiss, but instead of causing pleasure it causes cold) Perhaps if things had gone differently, and the Winter Kings eventually had assimilated into the larger Kindred community, other clans might have picked up a reflection of that power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T17:31:22-08:00","id":1166860,"title":"","content":"You know, it wouldn't surprise me if a Winter King kept a large retinue of Ghouls and young Childer still bound within the confines of Humanity (Bereschligost can potentially make that easier when you think about it), the better to watch over them as they slumber during the bright months. On the other hand, I can easily picture a Winter King pulling a 30 Days of Night on an isolated Siberian village; whilst their Discipline allows them to make do with animal blood, I'd imagine that mortal blood would still be much sweeter to them...and then the ensuing slaughter results in a few Revenants who can potentially serve as indentured labourers for the promise of uplifting...assuming no one drops a hint that Amaranth would accomplish the same thing. Perhaps such a habit caused karma to bite them in the backside.<br /> <br /> On a potentially deadly note, wouldn't this torpor make the Mikhaili more vulnerable to Strix possession? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11607-irontsim","name":"Irontsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11607_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T17:57:09-08:00","id":1166864,"title":"","content":"As it seems, if you assume the book as a whole (and not a collage of texts), I would address at least part of the messiness of the Dhampir chapter to their POV. It isn't so much that everything there is supposed to be true, but that it is supposed to be the true opinion of some well informed but still partial Dhampirs. It can be easily applied in the same degree to the Revenants to address any of their theories that contradict other sources. Sometimes it is still interesting to take the cWoD approach of &quot;unreliable narrator&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166718#post1166718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's it for now. I'm going to play Pokemon Go (gen 3 is out. Yay). See you next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't knew someone still played Pokemon Go. I'll maybe get back to it when I buy a new phone (my current one already have serious battery issues, I'll not get more than 12 minutes of playtime as it is). As a side note, I STd a game mixing CoD and Pok\u00e9mon, and the Kindred of the group was collecting Dark/Fire Types.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T06:41:01-08:00","id":1166976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166853#post1166853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also noticed the bit about the last Mikhaili creating a new clan, and the total absence of a follow-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impression that they didn't create a new clan so much as even their regular Embraces were now producing revenants rather than kindred.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:56:23-08:00","id":1166999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166976#post1166976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression that they didn't create a new clan so much as even their regular Embraces were now producing revenants rather than kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Gellydog refers to this sentence:<br /> &quot;And so, the Gangrel slaughtered the Winter Kings down to the last one, and that one fled <i>and started a new clan</i>, debased and powerless though it was.&quot; (Emphasis mine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T09:15:24-08:00","id":1167011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166999#post1166999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Gellydog refers to this sentence:<br /> &quot;And so, the Gangrel slaughtered the Winter Kings down to the last one, and that one fled <i>and started a new clan</i>, debased and powerless though it was.&quot; (Emphasis mine.)</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I referred to this in my review, and I assume that Gellydog did as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:49:22-08:00","id":1167044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166999#post1166999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe Gellydog refers to this sentence:<br /> &quot;And so, the Gangrel slaughtered the Winter Kings down to the last one, and that one fled <i>and started a new clan</i>, debased and powerless though it was.&quot; (Emphasis mine.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It begs the question of &quot;how does one start a new clan&quot; versus a bloodline. I hope this can be addressed in Spilled Blood, and that said book gives plenty of conflicting options for how things ended up &quot;this&quot; way.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:21:20-08:00","id":1167071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165098#post1165098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider: all three sub-splats are mixed up with vampires in a way that creates widely disparate power dynamics. That is, in other words, the entire focus of Masquerade: that the Undead Man is keeping you down and you'll never, ever be respected because you're like, a kid, ya'know--so burn it all down!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, though, is that the VtM parallels also extend to stuff like their interactions with other supernaturals -- in particular, the section on dhampir and werewolves seems to imply that there's a Classic WoD-style rivalry between werewolves and vampires again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T13:06:49-08:00","id":1167100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1166999#post1166999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Gellydog refers to this sentence:<br /> &quot;And so, the Gangrel slaughtered the Winter Kings down to the last one, and that one fled <i>and started a new clan</i>, debased and powerless though it was.&quot; (Emphasis mine.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the &quot;debased and powerless&quot; that made me think of revenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T15:05:14-08:00","id":1167148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167071#post1167071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, though, is that the VtM parallels also extend to stuff like their interactions with other supernaturals -- in particular, the section on dhampir and werewolves seems to imply that there's a Classic WoD-style rivalry between werewolves and vampires again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, also fully agreed. And without belaboring the point, CofD werewolves won't care about vamps or their half-breeds unless they impact kinfolk or the spirit-landscape. Vamps as evil buttheads is another game.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T15:22:58-08:00","id":1167155,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Kinfolk (both written and capitalised on page 47), isn't that the WtA version of Wolf-Blooded? That even further cements that someone couldn't separate WoD from CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T15:50:11-08:00","id":1167167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167155#post1167155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Kinfolk (both written and capitalised on page 47), isn't that the WtA version of Wolf-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T15:53:57-08:00","id":1167169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167155#post1167155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Kinfolk (both written and capitalised on page 47), isn't that the WtA version of Wolf-Blooded? That even further cements that someone couldn't separate WoD from CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. CofD never used the terminology Kinfolk, though the Wolf-Blooded started with pretty much the same concept. It isn't even that related anymore, and I like the new concept.<br /> <br /> But aside from seeming conflation of the two settings, by itself it could still be dismissed as personal habit. Some players I know still use Kinfolk in Forsaken for the sake of brevity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T15:58:14-08:00","id":1167171,"title":"","content":"If you want to talk about World of Darkness references in this book? &quot;Thin Blood.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T16:05:59-08:00","id":1167176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167171#post1167171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Thin Blood.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember seeing that in the book and a quick PDF search shows no results. Where was this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T16:17:21-08:00","id":1167178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167171#post1167171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to talk about World of Darkness references in this book? &quot;Thin Blood.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wrong with references, imo. The Mikhaili and the thinning of their blood is properly introduced in this book, and the sidebar for Bereschligost clarifies that it's either just a rumour or something that only happened to that particular clan (which is supported by the fact that the thinning of Mikhaili blood is represented by their clan bane). They've simply adopted a VtM concept into VtR with its own spin. I actually like that.<br /> <br /> The problem is when the writers starts referencing stuff from WoD that hasn't been established in CofD. The werewolf text seems like they references a relationship between werewolves and vampires that is true in WoD, but haven't been previously established in CofD. <i>That</i> becomes an inconsistency.<br /> <br /> In short; there's a difference between introducing concepts from WoD, and referencing WoD as if you were writing a WoD book. The former is borrowing material from one setting to expand another. The latter is mixing up two different settings, resulting in a mess that I'm wary of using as setting material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167176#post1167176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember seeing that in the book and a quick PDF search shows no results. Where was this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither does thinblood or thin-blood. Pretty sure they mean the lost clan Mikhaili.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-12-2017, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T16:45:19-08:00","id":1167181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167178#post1167178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing wrong with references, imo. The Mikhaili and the thinning of their blood is properly introduced in this book, and the sidebar for Bereschligost clarifies that it's either just a rumour or something that only happened to that particular clan (which is supported by the fact that the thinning of Mikhaili blood is represented by their clan bane). They've simply adopted a VtM concept into VtR with its own spin. I actually like that.<br /> <br /> The problem is when the writers starts referencing stuff from WoD that hasn't been established in CofD. The werewolf text seems like they references a relationship between werewolves and vampires that is true in WoD, but haven't been previously established in CofD. <i>That</i> becomes an inconsistency.<br /> <br /> In short; there's a difference between introducing concepts from WoD, and referencing WoD as if you were writing a WoD book. The former is borrowing material from one setting to expand another. The latter is mixing up two different settings, resulting in a mess that I'm wary of using as setting material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree 100%. I would have no idea that Mikhaili were a WoD reference without being told because it evolved organically from the text. In fact, that's one of my favourite parts of this book. The werewolf blurb is very clearly egregious because it references a relationship that doesn't exist beyond some allusions in Requiem 1e and is nowhere present in Foresaken or Requiem 2e. The first reference is awesome, the second one is a bummer for me. Its all in the execution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T21:07:08-08:00","id":1167219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167148#post1167148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, also fully agreed. And without belaboring the point, CofD werewolves won't care about vamps or their half-breeds unless they impact kinfolk or the spirit-landscape. Vamps as evil buttheads is another game.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they are Iron Masters- because, you know, Sacred Hunt and such. But yeah, it does feel more A than F.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T01:29:34-08:00","id":1167244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167219#post1167219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they are Iron Masters- because, you know, Sacred Hunt and such. But yeah, it does feel more A than F.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even most Iron Masters will be weary of vampires - looking for most troubling ones. Masters do not declare Sacred Hunt on any vamp they just see, don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T06:39:38-08:00","id":1167284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167219#post1167219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they are Iron Masters- because, you know, Sacred Hunt and such. But yeah, it does feel more A than F.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, and good catch, forum, on my use of &quot;kinfolk&quot; instead of proper wolf-blooded. WoD is the pervasive elephant in the setting room, and it has its own gravity....<br /> <br /> Back on that note: sure--there may be some werewolves, packs, lodges and even tribes that lean more toward &quot;cleanse them all and let Luna sort it out&quot;, but that's the aberration from the norm of &quot;vamps who?&quot; Similarly, you don't get vampire domains where the main sport is &quot;Lupine&quot; hunting, unless its specific to YOUR story and YOUR setting--likely with local repercussions.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T11:08:19-08:00","id":1167358,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Revenants- Part 2!</u></b><br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0cjZxJpfxa4\" target=\"_blank\">what I'm listening to while reading the chapter</a>- because everything is so dark that I need to balance it somehow :P )<br /> <br /> So if dhampirs are the eternal teenager, revenants are the eternal &quot;mistake&quot; who caused their mother to get stuck alone with a baby at 16 years old and hating her child for that? Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Again, capital Blood- was it also a thing in 2e and 100 years of night that I missed?<br /> <br /> Ooooooh. Dynasties. I like those. I really like how they are presented- a &quot;royalty among the debased&quot; and &quot;community among outcasts&quot;. Really cool concept.<br /> <br /> The revenant vampire slayer could be an even cooler antagonist than the dhampir one.<br /> <br /> Kind of weird how they moved from Dynasties to progenitor-revenant relationships. I can see the connection, but still, weird.<br /> <br /> Now, that was cool mini-fiction.<br /> <br /> The infectious nature of Vitae is truly examined in here. Nice.<br /> <br /> The danger of revenant creations suddenly becomes something that the usual Kindred really has to consider when they drink someone to death. Cool.<br /> <br /> Yeah, waking up as a revenant sounds scary as hell.<br /> <br /> So for revenants, you are either lucky- or dead.<br /> <br /> Seriously- how long is it that a revenant can pretend to be a normal person?<br /> <br /> I've thought that botch Embraces end up as Larvae- that is, like revenants, only perfectly mindless and hungry unless they diablerize someone. I guess things has changed? Also, it makes sense that a would be sire can't Uplift such revenants- but what stops them from pulling some strings and make another to preform the Uplifting for them? Or is it permanent? <br /> <br /> Really, all of those talking about &quot;thin blood&quot; and the stain on reputation and blood &quot;too weak&quot; to support a true vampire starts to make revenants sound like the new Caitiff. Is that a part of Requiem being old enough so she can go near Masquerade's house without waking up wondering how the bra came off? (credits to Rose for the quote).<br /> <br /> The italic texts seems like they have much more sense in those parts than in the previous ones. <br /> <br /> I know that I said it before, but I really do like how the communities of the revenants are presented.<br /> <br /> The example &quot;revenant meetings together for the first time&quot; also sounds really cool. The only thing that bugs me is that the first such example refers to the &quot;optional sidebar&quot; about the botch Embrace. I mean, it's ok to make it- but why the first? The first is usually the standard case, not the exception.<br /> <br /> Well, that's enough for now. I go back to watch that clip on repeat. See you :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T11:34:51-08:00","id":1167368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167358#post1167358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, capital Blood- was it also a thing in 2e and 100 years of night that I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T11:42:44-08:00","id":1167369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167368#post1167368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple times.</div> </div> </div> </div>makes sense. I do remember many references, but I've thought it was a fan term, not official one. I probably saw it once or twice- but I probably saw it as a metaphorical thing instead of some entity which is the manifestation of vampirehood. That the outcome of having some problems at focusing while reading long texts, especially when they lack some story structure. That's why I prefer my game books more as manuals instead of masses of words, so I can jump between sections without feel like reading the book drains the life out of me (hence why I just can't bring myself to read the Clan books or Secrets of the Covenants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T12:59:17-08:00","id":1167394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167358#post1167358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Revenants- Part 2!</u></b><br /> Really, all of those talking about &quot;thin blood&quot; and the stain on reputation and blood &quot;too weak&quot; to support a true vampire starts to make revenants sound like the new Caitiff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, yeah. That's an excellent observation, and now that there is a book explicitly supporting revenant play, I'd happily point someone who wants to be an outcast Caitiff their way. Revenants are no longer kill-on-sight walking problems for the Prince, but instead are potentially useful tools none the least of which is the mark of shame they represent for their creator. Marks of shame are hella useful in the All-Night Society.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thin blood&quot; is no longer a time linked to Gehenna, but what happens to someone when not enough of the curse gets through.... The Blood wants to spread.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T00:41:14-08:00","id":1167546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167369#post1167369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">makes sense. I do remember many references, but I've thought it was a fan term, not official one. I probably saw it once or twice- but I probably saw it as a metaphorical thing instead of some entity which is the manifestation of vampirehood. That the outcome of having some problems at focusing while reading long texts, especially when they lack some story structure. That's why I prefer my game books more as manuals instead of masses of words, so I can jump between sections without feel like reading the book drains the life out of me (hence why I just can't bring myself to read the Clan books or Secrets of the Covenants).</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have a theory about that, with the Curse infecting blood like a metaphysical virus that then causes the supernatural alterations and abilities we see in vampires and their related things like ghouls and dhampir. It's not so much that the Blood is a manifestation of vampirehood or a conscious entity that's exerting will on the setting as it's a meta origin for all vampire-like beings in the Chronicles of Darkness. It's a separate layer of supernatural biology that follows, loosely, the principles of evolution and speciation for vampires. It also serves as the binding glue between all of <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i>'s concepts in the same way that the existence of Spirits is for werewolves, or ghosts for Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> I think the Curse is always the same; it's a single magical...something from somewhere that was created or entered the world in the distant past. However, once it becomes the Blood, it can have a wide variety of effects and mutations. The Curse causes a few &quot;universal&quot; traits, like the intake of blood and the creation of Vitae and the animation of dead tissue. But it also reacts differently in different hosts, creating different &quot;species&quot; of vampire. Kindred vs. Jiang Shi vs. Strix (who could be the equivalent of patient zero for the Curse, having spread it into the mortal world, or are just another strain that found purchase in the ephemeral instead of the blood and tissue).<br /> <br /> The Blood passes down between sire and childe, creating bloodlines and clans as related groups of vampire that are all part of the same &quot;species.&quot; However, since all vampires spring from the same Curse, it's possible for vampires to share Blood and, thus, their unique powers and weaknesses. Do that enough between a large enough population, and you can actually blend &quot;species&quot; together until they become more similar than distinct. (Thus, the Kindred, five clans that have grown together enough to be considered a single(ish) body) The Jiang Shi in the Triangle are, in my opinion, a perfect (and deliberate...) example of a non-Kindred strain of vampire that's slowly being blended into the wider Kindred population. Give it enough time, and the Phantoms likely will be as similar to the Daeva or Ventrue as those two clans are to each other.<br /> <br /> So then you have things like ghouls, which are still-living organisms that are exposed to <i>just enough</i> of the Curse (via the Blood) to begin exhibiting its traits, while not being so overcome that they are totally transformed. A revenant is a vampire whose Blood doesn't contain enough of the Curse to stabilize itself in its new existence. Dhampir are created when magic allows a little bit of the Curse to pass to a child <i>without </i>the Blood, creating weird and unnatural (from the perspective of both normal life and the vampires' supernatural approximation of it) <br /> <br /> Anyway. The bottom line is that the Curse creates the Blood, and the Blood creates vampires. And vampires spread the Curse.. Everything else spins off from that. If that all makes sense...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:35:54-08:00","id":1167557,"title":"","content":"This chapter makes revenants seem a lot more common that I would have thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167546#post1167546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have a theory about that, with the Curse infecting blood like a metaphysical virus that then causes the supernatural alterations and abilities we see in vampires and their related things like ghouls and dhampir. It's not so much that the Blood is a manifestation of vampirehood or a conscious entity that's exerting will on the setting as it's a meta origin for all vampire-like beings in the Chronicles of Darkness. It's a separate layer of supernatural biology that follows, loosely, the principles of evolution and speciation for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had similar thoughts (comparing it to the Divine Fire relates to Prometheans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T05:47:33-08:00","id":1167583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167546#post1167546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. The bottom line is that the Curse creates the Blood, and the Blood creates vampires. And vampires spread the Curse.. Everything else spins off from that. If that all makes sense...</div> </div> </div> </div>You've written one of the more important short essays on the subject, and I think it or something like it needs to be in the Contagion Chronicle book. You've summed things up nicely and it also aligns with my own thoughts: that is, that the Curse entered the equation at some point, and after that has spread in various ways much as a mundane epidemic would, altering itself as needed via mutation to propagate better within constrained environments. It even has undesirable mutations manifesting under stress, such as &quot;thin blood&quot; or eventual aging (in one Bloodline example). <br /> <br /> The search for Patient Zero sounds like a fun, weird quest for a Mage/Vamp crossover. <br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to draw a parallel between the idea of the blood of the Tzimisce (WoD) being infected by Vicissitude, and the Curse of VtR. In fact, if you dispense with the literal Curse of Caine kind of thing, all that's left are biological models to draw on. And that's just fine!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:33:53-08:00","id":1167641,"title":"","content":"yeah, while reading through the book I've also started to have some cosmological thoughts along that line- only that I called the Curse as the Song, which is the concept of vampirisim as whole, while the Blood being the product of the first revenant starting a true Clan, creating- for the first time- the concept of &quot;Kindred&quot;. The Song stirs the Blood, and the Blood answers by absorbing more accursed beings into its line, turning them into a &quot;family&quot;, until it eventually falls from grace and is claimed by the Song once more. Of course, just as the Blood came from the Song, the Song also came from somewhere else- from the primordial silence from before life, and just as the Blood thickens and thins, so the Song would return to silence on night, and when that night would come, the Shadows would turn into Darkness, and engulf the world once more.<br /> <br /> But I have some very complex cosmological view for my CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:54:21-08:00","id":1167658,"title":"","content":"I always subscribed to the Ordo division - the Curse (banes and drawbacks), the Blood (vitae and its spreading) and Beast (vampy instincts, disciplines). <br /> <br /> The Blood is highly relevant here, in this book, because we're talking all about family here. The result of vitae being so infectious and spreading and transforming beings in different and unique ways. So, we're seeing more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T14:37:52-08:00","id":1167775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167557#post1167557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This chapter makes revenants seem a lot more common that I would have thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had that reaction, too. I think it might just be a consequence of the focused viewpoint- we're seeing things from the revenants' perspective, so we're seeing a more holistic view of their existence than the Kindred normally would give. We're talking about revenants, so we see a lot of revenants. The writeups do tend to give us the extreme version of things, so that we have more room to play around in. It does mention that there are far more Kindred than revenants, and I'd likely play it as permanent revenant &quot;societies&quot; being present only in the largest of cities with the most Kindred, with individuals and temporary groupings the best everywhere else can hope to sustain. Most Kindred probably will never meet a revenant, and consider them little more than urban legends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167658#post1167658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always subscribed to the Ordo division - the Curse (banes and drawbacks), the Blood (vitae and its spreading) and Beast (vampy instincts, disciplines).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not seen that breakdown before, but I really like it. It's almost a dark version of the mind/body/soul trifecta that often gets applied to humans in media such as <i>CofD</i>. The Beast is the mind, the Blood the body and the Curse the soul. All three things together make a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T16:03:14-08:00","id":1167787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167775#post1167775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not seen that breakdown before, but I really like it. It's almost a dark version of the mind/body/soul trifecta that often gets applied to humans in media such as <i>CofD</i>. The Beast is the mind, the Blood the body and the Curse the soul. All three things together make a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its from the <i>Rites of the Dragon</i> book and based on the original three coils - bane, beast and blood. <br /> <br /> Also, a bit drawn from the three aspects that the Belial's Brood talked about - <i>sarx, </i><i>soma</i>, and <i>pneuma. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T09:39:03-08:00","id":1167939,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Revenants- Part 3!</u></b><br /> Kinda straightforward title this time, ha?<br /> <br /> I must say that the all &quot;communities of the debased&quot; kind of thing really got my expectations high. Hope I won't be disappointed.<br /> <br /> Well, when you are a lot weaker than the competition, you have to learn how to work together, right?<br /> <br /> Kinda dig the all social structure examination. It is done in a good way, without becoming tiresome.<br /> <br /> Seriously, putting the emphasis upon revenant as pack hunters vs Kindred as lone predators makes a lot of sense, and grounds their place in the setting.<br /> <br /> I like the fact that this chapter keeps on presenting Kindred as both allies and antagonists. Much better than how they were presented in the previous chapter.<br /> <br /> I think that this section really emphasis why some revenants would prefer to avoid the Uplifting- sure, they'll get stuck cursed by hunger and frenzy and forever at the social ladder of the All Night Society no matter what they'll do (unless they'll take out the prince and put one of them in their place, a.k.a Cairo), but by doing so they'll forever lose that sense of community, having it replaced by the cold political constant backstabbing which is the vampire society.<br /> <br /> I do like the &quot;half damned together&quot; section- the fact that we all exist outside of the Kindred family doesnt mean we all need to love each other.<br /> <br /> Mortals and revenants- because you thought that Kindred and revenants have messy relationships.<br /> <br /> How do Blood Dolls manage to survive for more than, say, a couple of nights? Revenants aren't really famous for their self control, after all.<br /> <br /> Love the &quot;Revenant Secession&quot; sidebar. Really makes me think of Cairo.<br /> <br /> I think it is the first time in the book I stumbled upon the words &quot;Danse Macabre&quot;- which is sad. I love that expression in order to use the vampire politics.<br /> <br /> Finally- DYNSATIES<br /> <br /> Ceceya- new lost clan! woot woot!<br /> <br /> I would really be happy to see a vampire expansion to the Aztec Dark Era. As I know it won't happen, I may end up write a short example of one. I'll have to wait for Spilled Blood and see if it has anything to say about the Ceceya, Xotolol and that witch clan from Wicked Dead.<br /> <br /> Kinda disturbing that they resented the coming of the Spaniards in a kinda positive way- but it is hard to put the Aztecs on the &quot;good side&quot;, after all.<br /> <br /> The concept of &quot;new and strange vampires&quot; makes it feel like the clans of Mesoamerica were kinda different from the five common clans. I wonder what happened to them, and what happened to those clans in modern times. Still, the chances are they talk about the Ventrue. I wonder how much of Shadows of Mexico is still valid for 2e. Maybe we'll understand it better after Spilled Blood.<br /> <br /> Yeah, preforming an unholy magic in order to turn from a dhampir into a vampire- only to end as a revenant. Talking about a downgrade.<br /> <br /> Aztec Blood Magic- I wonder how that would look like?<br /> <br /> Revenant conspiracy in the health care? Sounds like the origin story of a Deviant.<br /> <br /> Apocalyptic revenant cult? Sounds legit. Or to put it in other words- &quot;Gehenna is coming! The Time of Thin Blood is upon us! The end is nigh! THE END IS NIGH!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> (I'm not even sorry. Well, a little bit)<br /> <br /> I wonder if the cult is actually a God Machine experiment. Sure, it doesn't have monopoly over Gnosticism, but it isn't that hard to play it that way.<br /> <br /> I must that I like how do the non clanish dynasties have a big emphasis about working with mortals. Makes a lot more of sense.<br /> <br /> Yeah, drug/human trafficking dynasty. The last link in the chain.<br /> <br /> Well, that looks like a good place to stop. I'll continue next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T11:54:45-08:00","id":1167980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167939#post1167939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Revenants- Part 3!</u></b><br /> How do Blood Dolls manage to survive for more than, say, a couple of nights? Revenants aren't really famous for their self control, after all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're not the only one that wonders this. In VtM you regained one dot of blood a day as a mortal. In CofD it's only represented as lethal damage, and that is healed at 1 per 2 days. <br /> <br /> So if you're a Blood Doll you need to frequently drag yourself out of the Rev nest you cuddle up with, to avoid being sucked dry after a night or two. Or, those Revs need to have some self-control at work; I suppose the latter is possible if they have the organization to establish a proper shelter and attract a herd like that.<br /> <br /> I still don't get why &quot;ooo Revs want to feed more often so I get my fix more&quot; is a thing as a Blood Doll. It's not like you can keep up with a normal Vamp, especially if they expend any energy on Disciplines!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T14:09:14-08:00","id":1168019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167546#post1167546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have a theory about that</div> </div> </div> </div>That made me really want to do a chronicle about searching for the origins and naturalistic explanations for supernatural phenomena.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167980#post1167980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not the only one that wonders this. In VtM you regained one dot of blood a day as a mortal. In CofD it's only represented as lethal damage, and that is healed at 1 per 2 days.<br /> <br /> So if you're a Blood Doll you need to frequently drag yourself out of the Rev nest you cuddle up with, to avoid being sucked dry after a night or two. Or, those Revs need to have some self-control at work; I suppose the latter is possible if they have the organization to establish a proper shelter and attract a herd like that.<br /> <br /> I still don't get why &quot;ooo Revs want to feed more often so I get my fix more&quot; is a thing as a Blood Doll. It's not like you can keep up with a normal Vamp, especially if they expend any energy on Disciplines!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of some Blood Dolls surviving quite some time, though it certainly would not be the most common thing to happen. A BD don't need to be the only, or even the first bite of a Revenant, much less do it every night. A smart one can manage to be on the safe side with things like push someone else in first. Don't think about a vampire that don't dry the source, but one that take steps to not dry a specific favored source.<br /> <br /> Overall it seems they got something very interesting for Revenants here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T14:53:59-08:00","id":1168027,"title":"","content":"I find it notable that blood dolls aren't actually addicted to the Kiss unless 1) special circumstances determined by the ST, or 2) Kiss of the Succubus merit, or 3) slipping a bit of vitae into the mix.<br /> <br /> Blood dolls suffer from a persistant Swooned, and often end up dealing with Wanton/Bestial/Competative, but they're not there jonsing for a fix usually. At least not from a strict reading of the rules; STs can always rule otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - perhaps notable isn't the right word. Strange is closer, but not right either; I don't find it strange, but there is a bit of odd dissonance whenever it comes up, but that's not how the game is working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-15-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T14:47:20-08:00","id":1168252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167939#post1167939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, putting the emphasis upon revenant as pack hunters vs Kindred as lone predators makes a lot of sense, and grounds their place in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked this, too. After all the focus on revenants creating little communities and finding &quot;stability,&quot; I was wondering what made them so different than just &quot;hungrier Kindred.&quot; Playing them up as the wild dogs sniffing around the leopard's territory helps give them a place in <i>Reqiuem'</i>s &quot;ecosystem&quot; that is unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T15:26:04-08:00","id":1168258,"title":"","content":"A Dampyr with the right merits and Crauc \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, and the right rite can create a Blood God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T15:10:57-08:00","id":1171639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1167939#post1167939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that looks like a good place to stop. I'll continue next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You ok, or just away for Christmas?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T23:14:28-08:00","id":1171740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1171639#post1171639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You ok, or just away for Christmas?</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, and unfortunately, it is not Christmas. It is just that the workload from my university was so great, that I barely even noticed that the week has passed, not top mention having time to return and read Half Damned. Hope things would become easier next week. Thank you for your interest!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or 